      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Cellular and brain metabolism of dopamine can be correlated with a number of neurodegenerative disorders, our study was to explore a simple and efficient method to detect dopamine in real samples."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "A new quantum dots (CdTe QDs) could be prepared using the hydrothermal method, the electrochemical biosensor was established by dropping CdTe QDs on the surface of glassy carbon electrode (GCE)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "The CdTe QDs/GCE exhibited the excellent electrochemical catalytic activity toward dopamine (DA) with good stability and high sensitivity in presence of interfering substances. The detection limit of DA was calculated by differential pulse voltammetry (DPV) as low as 0.3 μmol L-1 with a linear dynamic range of 1 μmol L-1 to 400 μmol L-1 ."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "In this paper, the proposed electrochemical biosensor could be effectively used for the direct and rapid detection of DA in human serum and urine samples."
          }
        ]
      },
